Among with the translations there are also rotations:
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
t^{'} \\
x^{'}
\end{pmatrix} =
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos \theta & \sin \theta \\
-\sin \theta & \cos \theta
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
t \\
x
\end{pmatrix}
$$
Look, for example, at the first row. After defining $v = \tan \theta$, it is actually the $t$ transformation, with $\kappa = 1$:
$$
